In this learning path, you'll:

1. Plan automation of your software development life cycle with GitHub Actions workflows.
2. Use GitHub Actions to automatically build your application.
3. Use GitHub Script to interact with the GitHub API.
4. Publish automatically and securely your code libraries or Docker images with GitHub Packages.

IT department wants to automate creating and tearing down the project's infrastructure. 
You decide to use continuous integration (CI) and continuous delivery (CD) to automate all the build, test, and deployment tasks.
You're also going to adopt infrastructure as code (IaC) to automate the IT tasks.

some modules are:

>> Learn what GitHub Actions are, the types of actions, and where to find them.
>> Identify the required components within a GitHub Actions workflow file.
>> Plan the automation of your software-development lifecycle with GitHub Actions workflows.
>> Create a container action and have it run in a workflow that's triggered by a push event to your GitHub repository.
